  "question": {
    "text": "Let $p, q$ and $r$ be the side4s opposite to the angles $P, Q$ and $R,$ respectively in a $\\Delta P Q R$. Then, $2 p r \\sin \\left(\\frac{p-Q+R}{2}\\right)$ equals",
