  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In $\\Delta P Q R, P+Q+R=180^{\\circ}$\r\n$\\begin{aligned} \\therefore 2 p r \\sin \\left(\\frac{P-Q+R}{2}\\right) &=2 p r \\sin \\frac{180^{\\circ}-Q-Q}{2} \\\\ &=2 p r \\sin \\left(90^{\\circ}-Q\\right) \\\\ &=2 p r \\cos Q \\\\=&\\left(\\quad \\ln \\Delta P Q R \\cos Q=\\frac{p^{2}+r^{2}-q^{2}}{2 p r}\\right) \\\\=& 2 p r\\left(\\frac{p^{2}+r^{2}-q^{2}}{2 p r}\\right)=p^{2}+r^{2}-q^{2} \\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
